DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(1/(x))/6");
$fun_1 = Formula("3/(((x^5)^2))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("[1, 11] U [1, 11]");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-10, 2} - ((-infinity, infinity) - [1, 11]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [1, 11])");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("[1, 11] U [1, 11] U [1, 11]");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("({-10, -4, 3, 4} - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-10, -4, 3, 4}))) U [4, infinity)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("[4, infinity) U {-10, -4, 3, 4} U [4, infinity)");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("[4, infinity) U ({-10, -4, 3, 4}) U [4, infinity) U [4, infinity)");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`7+2+16`]? [_____]{answer=>25,width=>10}
---

[`9+7*15`] is equal to [_____]{114}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \geq 4\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, -4, 3, 4\}`]

Compute:
- [`(B \cap (B)) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`A \cup (B) \cup A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 1 \leq x \leq 11\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, 2\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cap A \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`A \cup A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -3, 4, -2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -6, -6, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 5, -6, 8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, -6, 2>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<5, -6, 8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, -6, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, 4, -2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 2, -4, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -4, 2, -3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 9, 4, 2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-4, 2, -3>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<2, -4, 10>") x Compute("<9, 4, 2>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<2, -4, 10>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<9, 4, 2>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
